# GitHub language statistics.
#
# Goal: the bar should describe the code we actually wrote — the Rust tunnel core
# and the Kotlin Android client — not the third-party C we vendored to build it.
#
# Vendored (excluded from the stats):
#   core/quiche              Cloudflare's QUIC/HTTP-3 library (4.5 MB of Rust)
#   app/src/main/cpp/badvpn  badvpn tun2socks + lwIP TCP/IP stack (3.1 MB of C)
#
# Ours (counted):
#   core/aether/src          the MSN-GUARD Rust core
#   app/src/main/java        the MSN-GUARD Kotlin client
#   app/src/main/cpp/*.cpp   our JNI bridge

core/quiche/** linguist-vendored
app/src/main/cpp/badvpn/** linguist-vendored

# Generated protocol/parser sources inside the vendored tree.
*.y linguist-generated
*.l linguist-generated

# Documentation should not be counted as code.
docs/** linguist-documentation
*.md linguist-documentation

# Keep text files normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.apk binary
*.so binary
